  "caveats": [
    "The cause is a hypothesis. A university-calendar change is the leading candidate; it is not established, and the component is a measured gap, not an attribution.",
    "The prior analysis (D70-D74) read 2026 as inside India's historical range on level-free measures. This component rests on the decision that a twelve-week run above the four-year envelope is a real-world effect to carry, not noise to revert.",
    "The `settle` half-life is a planning constant. The `fade` half-life is fitted, but on deviations that were noise; it says how fast India reverts when nothing is driving it, which is exactly what `fade` assumes.",
    "The `l` share used for netting is the August cycle's. The September run will recompute it on fresher training data; it moves by tenths of a point.",
    "The norm is a flat four-year mean. India's seasonal amplitude has been flattening year over year (LOO gap +1.29 in 2025), so part of the gap is drift that predates 2026. Brendan chose the flat norm knowingly."
  ],
